WEBVTT

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.860
Kanyou

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.200
Report!

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.830
K-Kankoku Pass is standing strong!

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.410
Ka Rin: A Spirited Woman

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.540
Our dogged defense continues!

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.960
Yes! We did it!

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.500
Imagine the shock if they'd
breached it on day one!

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.170
I want detailed reports
on each battlefield.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.170
Sir!

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.680
First two massive Gi siege towers
placed ladders on Kankoku Pass.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.890
Wh-What?!

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.310
General Kan Ki burned one of them down.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.440
Got to hand it to that mountain bandit.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.530
General Chou Tou stood firm
until the other tower withdrew.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.160
That's Chou Tou for you!

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.070
"En" "Chin"

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.830
Ou Sen's army is guarding
the left mountains

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.040
and keeping the opposing En army at bay.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.540
Very good.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.000
Meanwhile, General Tou himself
took to the right battlefield

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.720
and promptly eliminated one
of So's three generals!

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.930
M-My goodness! Is this true?

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.680
And Mou Bu?

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.850
There's been no movement
from Mou Bu's army.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.600
Excellent.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.230
We've killed one general while preserving
our main force, the Mou Bu Army.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.780
This is big!

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.240
Finally, on the rightmost battlefield,
where Lord Hyou's army

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.070
saw the fiercest fighting
of the first day...

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:40.120
Despite a large number of casualties,
General Man Goku of Sho was defeated!

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.290
Heavens! They killed a general
on that battlefield, too?

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:51.670
Man Goku--is he the fellow we wanted
kept away from Kanyou?

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.550
That's him.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.100
More excellent news! And the one
who killed him--was it Lord Hyou?

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.430
Er, no. It was battalion commander
Shin of the Hi Shin Force.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.440
Wha--?!

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.030
Y-Your Highness?!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.160
It's nothing.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.870
Now for the damage sustained by each army.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:23.790
Lord Hyou's army has been reduced
by ten thousand troops...

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.530
Shin...

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.000
You really will save us.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.210
We should be whooping it up, dammit!

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.840
That was one hell of an accomplishment,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.680
but Man Goku had to go on
about Battle of Chouhei and curses.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:44.940
That white-haired guy... he looked like
the man who killed my brother.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.810
Oh, did he?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:53.240
But after hearing all that, I don't know
if I have a grudge against the guy.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.650
Just look at our commander.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.660
He took down a general--he should
be the happiest one here.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:06.210
Argh! It's no use! We did great out there,
but our morale's way low!

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.130
Whoa!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.180
--What the hell?!
--He kissed her! That was a kiss!

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.390
Let's drink, boy!

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.110
Nights are for getting drunk
on the sweet wine of victory.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.450
That's the best part of being in battle!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.630
Drink up, boy.
You're the hero of the hour!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:28.310
Or will you grieve this world and cry
all night long, out of pity for Man Goku?

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:31.940
I suppose warriors like that
are amusing in their own way.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.530
Well? My liquor is outstanding, is it not?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:50.450
Why, it even took old Ou Ki by surprise!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.330
I ain't done yet!

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.300
By the way, Shin...

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.140
You did a fine job commanding those
10,000 troops at the rear.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.680
Opportunistic, yes--

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.930
but that was a forceful flame
that unleashed the very wind.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:19.070
Still, this battlefield started with
120,000 versus 40,000.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:22.690
Killing Man Goku doesn't
change that power differential.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.410
I reckon both sides have lost
about 10,000 apiece.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:31.200
So if both sides keep losing troops
at this rate, Chin will be wiped out.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.870
What's the outlook on
the battle going forward?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:39.210
War is a living thing.
We can't tell until it's underway.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.970
But one thing is crucial:

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:50.310
Whether the firestarter can show
up where the fire will be lit.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.810
I don't get it.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:59.900
I think... I maybe kinda understand
"where the fire will be lit."

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.490
And we absolutely can't leave that spot.

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:07.280
How many have you lost?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.580
About 300.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.580
I'll replace them with
300 of my own men.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.950
Huh?!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.500
Plus another two 500-man
squadrons to help you out.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.380
They're all yours--though they're
outrageously boorish.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:26.130
B-But why would you...

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.890
Just a hunch.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.640
Huh?

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:33.060
This is no time to be wallowing
in silly sentimentality.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:36.600
A country's life is hanging
in the balance!

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.900
This war is where you
transform, Shin, my boy.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.690
If you don't,

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.240
this battlefield will be beyond intense!

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.620
Just what I like to hear!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.580
To be honest, losing Man Goku is a blow.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:04.090
His very existence was
helpful in so many ways.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.170
Him and that deranged face of his.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.260
I am ashamed.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:14.220
I heard that Lord Hyou was <i>not</i>
the one who did the deed.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:19.390
No. Suddenly another firestarter has
appeared, apart from Lord Hyou.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.400
Apart from Lord Hyou?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.780
Shin, the 1,000-man commander
of the Hi Shin Force.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:34.200
What a surprise. To think he'd kill Man Goku,
the very nemesis of the Chin army...

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:38.500
War does greatly hasten one's
growth and development.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:42.170
Will this battle spur him on even further?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.590
Rin Bu Kun...

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.640
Set it alight!

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:52.640
Sir!

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:59.100
This sure as hell ain't over.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.100
You'll see, Rin Bu Kun!

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:06.020
I'll tear Tou's guts right
outta his belly!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.610
Long live Rin Bu Kun!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.360
Hear, hear!

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.070
Death to the Chin army!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.820
Death!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.620
Death to the Chin army!

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.160
Death!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.080
Death to the Chin army!

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.790
Death!

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:23.710
To Rin Bou.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.960
Thus the first battles ended.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:32.340
The night stretched on quietly, each side
keeping a watchful eye on the other.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.300
Day 2, Early Morning

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.430
Day 2 arrived.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.770
Is So putting Kan Mei out there already?

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:45.190
No, we'll dispatch the second army first.

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:50.110
You know, I have hardly any intel
on the second army's commander.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.990
Mostly that they came up
the ranks only recently.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.080
What kind of general are we talking about?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.330
One with a...

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:02.620
A problematic personality, let's say.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.750
Why would a warrior like that
lead the second army?

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.840
Why else?

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.590
She's a battle genius.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:17.140
Rounding up the leaders of the losing
armies like this... What's the plan?

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:21.390
Who knows. At any rate, we'll be
absorbed into the second army.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.270
Hey!

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:25.770
Here comes that lady general
we've been hearing about.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.440
I hear she's petite--and a real looker.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.440
Knock it off, Yoku.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.650
<i>I </i>hear she's dangerous even
when she's on your side.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.320
She won't appreciate your
jokes like Rin Bu Kun did.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.920
Sh-She's <i>huge</i>!

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:47.880
As big as Kan Mei!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:52.380
Second So Army

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:51.630
So this is the second
army general: Ka Rin!

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:56.550
Which one of you is
Rin Bu Kun's adjutant, Ro Kin?

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.800
Here! I am.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.850
I am honored to serve the second--

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.690
Wh-What did you <i>do</i>?!

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.650
Ro Kin!

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:12.230
I have no use for bald,
grubby-handed good-for-nothings.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.990
Loser swine.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:15.650
Say <i>what</i>?!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:16.610
Yoku!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:20.450
Normally I'd be disposing
of you all right now.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.200
You swine are only alive because
the high commander is nearby.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.830
But you get only one day's respite.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.210
I've decided my second
army will not mobilize.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.720
You'll fight on your own today.

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:39.550
And if you can't manage
to kill General Tou of Chin,

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.720
I'll behead every last one of you.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.810
Wha--

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:47.100
If I give you a chance, the high
commander can hardly get angry.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:54.940
Oh, and... not a single
word about my height.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.280
Heads <i>will </i>roll.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.280
Later.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.400
Day 2: So Army vs. Mou Bu's & Tou's Allied Army

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.700
Dammit! Fighting without a commander?!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.870
How can we take down a general
with no strategy--no nothing?

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.840
Is the second army seriously
not making a move?!

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:13.210
They're not budging!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.300
Shit! Is that giantess really gonna
watch from the sidelines?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:23.600
The former first army is out there with
no commander, just slugging away.

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.890
What's going on?

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.720
"Mou"

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.020
I can't get a read on what
the foe means to do.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:33.940
Report from the Sho battlefield!
No major changes in either army!

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:38.530
Lord Hyou has remained with the main
camp and is observing each battle!

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:41.660
That's because he knows
Kei Sha can take him.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:45.120
And Chin has no reason
to hurry things along.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.450
Report from the En battlefield!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:51.130
"En"

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:51.130
The En army is continuing its assault
on Ou Sen's stronghold,

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.340
but there's still no sign of it falling!

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:57.760
I saw the stronghold Ou Sen
built in Sanyou.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:01.840
En's battlefield may not see
much action anytime soon.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.300
Besides...

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.810
Now that Gi's taken
their siege towers away,

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:09.390
this has become a
routine castle-wall assault.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:12.810
If anyone makes a
move today, it'll be So's...

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:16.110
Urgent report from the So battlefield!

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.690
The day is half over!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:20.820
No movement whatsoever
from So's second army!

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:21.820
What?!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.030
"Chin" "So"

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.200
Are you sure about this?

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.410
Isn't this bad for the So army,
coming so soon

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:33.000
after Rin Bu Kun's blunder
on the first day?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.790
Shut up.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:38.380
Day two and beyond are all mine.
Orders are orders.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.590
Can't do anything about that.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.890
K-Kan Mei, sir!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.140
What do you think you're doing, Ka Rin?

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.560
Your actions may well be unforgivable!

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.160
Why aren't you mobilizing the second army?
I want a concise answer.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.830
I hated that old baldy.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.830
I'm tormenting his underlings. What of it?

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.580
Bare your neck, Ka Rin.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:22.340
Don't get so overheated, Master Kan Mei.
It was just a joke--a joke.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:26.470
Why aren't they mobilized?
You have five seconds.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.390
It's called "strategy."

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:37.690
And you can kill a Chin general
with these unconventional tactics?

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:38.730
Don't be ridiculous.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:45.360
This strategy isn't meant for
small fry like Chin generals.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.780
Then what?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.830
<i>This </i>strategy is for taking Kankoku Pass.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.750
Wait--Ka Rin has advice for <i>us</i>?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.130
Yes...

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.380
Please share it.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:03.420
"Have the other armies
continue their mediocre battles,

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.590
and in ten days, Kankoku Pass will be ours."

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:11.770
With ten days of mediocre battles?

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:15.640
Ri Boku.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.400
I see.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:22.320
So's second-army general,
Ka Rin--she's the real deal.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.200
"En" "Ou"

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:35.210
Sir! The first wave is falling behind!

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.670
And the left sidewall is under attack!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:42.250
Things are finally getting
interesting around here.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.630
Ou Sen! Your stronghold
is a fine one, to be sure.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:49.930
But the Ordo Army
with its northern mountain folk

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:54.140
happens to be particularly skilled
in storming mountain castles!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.390
A message! A message!

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:57.900
Eh?

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:01.390
"Sho"

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:01.820
A war of attrition?
Do we have a timeframe?

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:03.400
Ten to 20 days.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:09.110
Call off Kou Son Ryuu's charge.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.120
Sir!

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.490
"Gi"

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.160
A simple war of attrition...

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:16.990
"Kan"

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.500
Leave it to Ri Boku.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.250
He understands.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.170
Push on through, Hi Shin Force!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.590
"Hi"

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:32.760
Day 2 saw none of the huge
battle upsets of the first day.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:37.770
Armies kept fighting on every battlefield,
chipping away at each other's forces

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:40.400
as offense and defense were no more.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.060
"So" "Chin"

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:47.650
So the first army is the only
one out here? Again?

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:52.530
And <i>she </i>thinks we oughta be grateful
we still have our heads!

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:56.750
We'll never avenge Rin Bu Kun like this!

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.460
Day 3 passed in much the same fashion.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.880
Do ya get the feeling Sho's been quieter
'n usual these past couple days?

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.430
Huh?!

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:12.850
How so? We're getting <i>clobbered </i>out there!

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:16.310
Sure beats the first day, though!

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.640
What's your take, Ten?

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.480
Huh?

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:26.230
Ya dirty-minded brat!
You're all awkward now--'cause of <i>that</i>?

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.190
Hey, Shin, you jerk!

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.650
What are you doing to our tactician?!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.870
Ow! Is that any way to treat
your commanding officer?

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:39.200
You're concerned about the coalition
army's movements these past two days?

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.710
I am.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.460
It feels as though they've changed tactics

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:47.210
after the results of
the first day's battles.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:53.010
I'm more concerned that all of the
coalition armies are doing the same thing.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:56.510
If the coalition army had
a weakness to exploit,

00:17:56.510 --> 00:18:00.980
it would be that it was
roughly cobbled together.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:05.860
For a patchwork army to be in sync
like this is quite troublesome.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:07.730
Indeed.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:13.240
That said, we're only three days in.
I may be overthinking this.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:18.160
You're not overthinking anything.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:23.500
After all, we <i>are </i>up against Ri Boku,
the man who killed Ou Ki.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:24.500
Mmm.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.380
It's just so strange!

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:34.590
The fate of our country rests on
Kankoku Pass, with only us to guard it.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.220
And we're not even among the Six Greats!

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.520
I hated those guys.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.390
Me, too.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:52.650
Well, longevity may be a talent,
of a sort.

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:57.320
We've certainly beaten
them in that regard.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.700
Indeed.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:04.670
Old generals have roles
only old generals can fill.

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:06.460
Roles?

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:10.590
Ou Sen and my son Bu
can provide the talent.

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:14.130
They can hold their own with
the Six Greats in that regard.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.850
Yet those two cannot defend Kankoku Pass.

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.720
Why do you think that is?

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.020
They lack <i>heft</i>.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:30.150
That's what defending our
national gate is all about!

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:35.950
Which is why the genius Shou Hei Kun
stationed us on Kankoku Pass.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:40.330
Us and Kan Ki,
Chin's shrewdest general, that is.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.290
Indeed.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:45.500
I take it as a sign from the heavens.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:50.670
They've prepared quite the important
stage for us two old soldiers.

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:54.970
Let us both etch our names into
the annals of history, Chou Tou!

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:57.130
I could ask for nothing more.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.800
"Chin"

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:03.850
Day 4 and still no major movement, eh?

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:09.230
How long will the enemy's main camp
remain watching from the sidelines?

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:15.650
Though with provisions not an issue,
we'd actually prefer a drawn-out battle.

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:23.080
Another two days came and went.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.670
Then, on the morning of the seventh day...

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:32.960
It's about that time.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:36.510
Tell the Gi army to clear a path.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:40.340
Commanding General of Kan
Sei Kai

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:40.090
And if they get caught up
in this, don't blame us.

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:47.100
Hmm? The Kan army's moving forward!

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:50.520
So Commanding General Sei Kai
is mobilizing at last.

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.650
Boss! Something's different!

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.900
What's that? What the heck is that?!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:21:01.030
Huh? What <i>is </i>that?
Go on, get out of here!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:21:01.030
Let it go. They're not coming here.
And calm down, O Gi Ko.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.370
The Kan army, on the move?

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:06.870
It hardly matters who. Shoot them down!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:10.580
Sei Kai, sir, we're within range.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.210
Begin.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:27.640
Idiots. The high ground has an
overwhelming advantage in an arrow fight!

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:34.770
C-Captain?!

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.450
Ch-Chou Tou, sir, is this--

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:44.030
The toxic weaponry unit.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:46.030
Toxic... weapons?

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:50.620
B-But can there be a poison
that works so quickly?

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.830
It's no poison we would know of.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.300
Sei Kai sets out for strange worlds,

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:59.420
south beyond Etsu and
west beyond Kyoudo,

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:03.510
collecting highly poisonous plants,
animals, and minerals.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:10.480
He studies them day and night, creating a
range of unique and toxic weapons.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:16.320
Apparently Sei Kai was once a beauty,
turning even other men's heads.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:20.940
But to look at him now...

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:23.490
The fate of a poisonsmith.

00:22:23.490 --> 00:22:26.490
In the course of his research,
he, too, was poisoned.

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:29.700
There's not a single healthy man
in his command.

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:32.370
Sei Kai himself has been transfigured

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:35.670
into this beastly, dark-veined apparition.

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:39.460
Such is the price that's been paid
for Sei Kai's concoctions.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:42.170
This is no ordinary poison, Chin!

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:49.060
Poison arrows!

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:52.520
All units, move out beyond
the arrows' reach!

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.730
There you are, Chin commander.

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:05.360
Careful!

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:06.530
I know!

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:11.450
They're targeting you, Chou Tou!

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:14.420
Bring the injured inside
and tend to their wounds!

00:23:14.420 --> 00:23:15.620
Do it.

00:24:52.510 --> 00:25:02.020
Mou Bu's Declaration

00:24:54.180 --> 00:24:58.190
Next time on<i> Kingdom</i>:
"Mou Bu's Declaration."
